From 39f603e3da8e86c62f04984f729174d2c0123e5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 11:35:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Shorten the blank stretch at the end of the hero dive
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measured on a 390×844 phone: the veil is fully opaque from hero progress
0.6 to 1.0, and at a pin length of 190% that was 642px of blank cream to
scroll through before the categories began to emerge — most of a screen of
nothing, one whole swipe on a phone.

The pin now ends at 130%. The progress-to-scale curve and the veil's
timings are untouched, so the veil still closes at the same scale — the
Safari safeguard in CLAUDE.md §3 holds exactly as before (scale 1.91 and
veil 0.31 at progress 0.45, both runs). Only the scroll per unit of
progress changed: the blank stretch measures 439px now.

Invariants unchanged at 1280×800, 390×844 and 390×600: scale 11, lens
offset 0/0, pin gap 0, no console errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EzyC6nrRn89wkcu7EDPwMW
---
 script.js | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/script.js b/script.js
index db8292a..344e21b 100644
--- a/script.js
+++ b/script.js
@@ -615,7 +615,15 @@ function buildHomeMotion() {
       scrollTrigger: {
         trigger: "#hero",
         start: "top top",
-        end: "+=190%",
+        /* How much scroll the dive takes. The progress-to-scale curve and the
+           veil's timing below are untouched by this figure, so the veil still
+           closes at the same scale — what changes is only how far a thumb
+           travels to get there. At 190% the veil was fully opaque from
+           progress 0.6 to 1.0: on a 390×844 phone that was 642px of blank
+           cream before the categories began to emerge, most of a screen of
+           nothing. At 130% the same stretch measures 440px. Below about
+           120% the entry itself starts to feel cut short. */
+        end: "+=130%",
         scrub: 0.5,
         pin: true,
         anticipatePin: 1,
-- 
2.43.0

